            <p style="text-align:left;font-weight:bold;">(H) Operation Procedure for Commissioning:</p>
              <table cellpadding="4">
        <tr>
                                   <th style="width:6%;">Sr. No.</th>
            <th style="width:60%;">Preparatory Work</th>
            <th style="width:20%;">Action by</th>
            <th style="width:14%;">Check</th>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td class="center">1</td>
            <td>
                Inform HOD (O&amp;M), HOD (Steel &amp; CNG Projects GA1 &amp; GA2)
                &amp; Emergency team about commencement of NRO.
            </td>
            <td class="center">O&amp;M Engineer &amp;<br/>Project Engineer</td>
            <td></td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td class="center">2</td>
            <td>
                Ensure O&amp;M and Project manpower is present on site at NRO location.
            </td>
            <td class="center">O&amp;M Engineer &amp;<br/>Project Engineer</td>
            <td></td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td class="center">3</td>
            <td>Check communication facility with all personnel.</td>
            <td class="center">O&amp;M Engineer</td>
            <td></td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td class="center">4</td>
            <td>
                Ensure compliance to all related MGL Life Saving Rules
                before &amp; during NRO.
            </td>
            <td class="center">Project Engineer /<br/>O&amp;M Engineer</td>
            <td></td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td class="center">5</td>
            <td>
                Ensure specific site risk assessment to be conducted
                before commencement of commissioning.
            </td>
            <td class="center">O&amp;M / Project Engineer</td>
            <td></td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td class="center">6</td>
            <td>
                Check for any potential sources of ignition in the vicinity
                of valve V7 &amp; V9 and remove if found any.
            </td>
            <td class="center">O&amp;M Technician /<br/>Engineer</td>
            <td></td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td class="center">7</td>
            <td>
                Install vent stack and flame arrestor with earthing arrangement at V10.
                Also install digital pressure gauge at vent valve V10.
            </td>
            <td class="center">O&amp;M / Project Engineer</td>
            <td></td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td class="center">8</td>
            <td>
                Remove BLRF of 2&quot; valve spool at location B using non-sparking tools.
                Check for gas passing from valve V7 at location A.
                If gas passing is observed, follow contingency procedure (page no. 11).
            </td>
            <td class="center">O&amp;M Technician /<br/>Engineer</td>
            <td></td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td class="center">9</td>
            <td>
                If gas is not passing through V7, connect 2&quot; WNRF of spur line
                with vent valve spool piece using non-sparking tools.
                Provide spade in 2&quot; WNRF assembly for positive isolation.
            </td>
            <td class="center">O&amp;M Technician /<br/>Engineer</td>
            <td></td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td class="center">10</td>
