            <p style="text-align:left;font-weight:bold;">(I) Contingency Action Plan:</p>
                      <p> If, Passing of Valve V7:-</p>
                      
              <table cellpadding="1">
        <tr>
            <th style="width:10%;">Sr. No</th>
            <th style="width:80%;">Action Plan</th>
            <th style="width:10%;">Responsibility</th>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td class="center">1</td>
            <td>Inform emergency team and control room about the passing of Valve V7.</td>
            <td class="center">O&amp;M Engineer</td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td class="center">2</td>
            <td>Close valves V1 (8&quot;) &amp; V4 (8&quot;).</td>
            <td class="center">O&amp;M Engineer</td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td class="center">3</td>
            <td>
                Check source of ignition in vicinity of valve V3 &amp; V5, remove if found any.
                Remove BLRF from V5 and connect vent stack with flame arrestor at V5.
                Depressurize the line section by opening valve V5.
            </td>
            <td class="center">O&amp;M Technician / Engineer</td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td class="center">4</td>
            <td>
                Connect the nitrogen hose assembly at V3.
                Open valve V3 &amp; start nitrogen purging from V5.
            </td>
            <td class="center">O&amp;M Technician / Engineer</td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td class="center">5</td>
            <td>
                Check percentage of gas at valve V5.
                Stop nitrogen purging when the level falls below the safe limit and issue hot work permit.
                Ensure 00 PPM.
                If still gas passing is observed, abandon the NRO and inform HOD (O&amp;M),
                emergency team and control room.
            </td>
            <td class="center">O&amp;M Technician / Engineer</td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td class="center">6</td>
            <td>
                If gas is not passing, cold cut the affected pipeline section by hacksaw
                and weld prefabricated spool piece with 2&quot; valve.
            </td>
            <td class="center">O&amp;M Technician / Engineer</td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td class="center">7</td>
            <td>Conduct NDT of weld joints. Close valves V5 &amp; V3.</td>
            <td class="center">Project Engineer</td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td class="center">8</td>
            <td>
                Re-commission the network using bypass hoses (SS 300#) between valve V2 &amp; V3
                (as per correct practice) and check the % of gas at V5 and V11 using vent stack
                with flame arrestor arrangement.
                Continue until obtaining three consecutive readings of gas percentage in excess of 95%,
                as per COP section-8.
            </td>
            <td class="center">Project Engineer</td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td class="center">9</td>
            <td>
                Allow the section to get fully pressurized by monitoring through pressure gauge at V8.
                Fully open the valves V1 &amp; V4.
            </td>
            <td class="center">O&amp;M Technician / Engineer</td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td class="center">10</td>
            <td>
                Install BLRF at valves V3, V5, V8 &amp; V11 and perform leak test.
            </td>
            <td class="center">O&amp;M Technician</td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td class="center">11</td>
            <td>
                Restore the valves to their original position as per table
